ency is confirmed.\n- **Lifelong steroid replacement** with stress dose adjustments.\n\n### **Why Not the Other Options?**\n- **(C) Start androgen replacement** → Not indicated in acute adrenal crisis.\n- **(B) IV fludrocortisone alone** → Does not address cortisol deficiency.\n- **(D) Start both hydrocortisone and fludrocortisone immediately** → Fludrocortisone is not always needed upfront; cortisol deficiency is the immediate priority.\n- **(E) ACTH stimulation test** → Diagnostic but **not urgent**—this patient needs **immediate treatment**.\n\n### **Final Answer: (A) Administer intravenous hydrocortisone** to stabilize the patient before further diagnostic workup.', tool_calls=Unset(), prefix=False, role='assistant')]
